# API Contract: Textbook Search Tool

## Overview
The `search_textbook` tool allows the OpenAI Agent to retrieve relevant textbook content when answering student questions.

## Tool Definition
```json
{
  "type": "function",
  "function": {
    "name": "search_textbook",
    "description": "Search the Physical AI & Humanoid Robotics textbook for relevant content to answer student questions",
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "query": {
          "type": "string",
          "description": "The student's question or topic to search for in the textbook"
        }
      },
      "required": ["query"]
    }
  }
}
```

## Expected Behavior
- Input: A query string from the OpenAI Agent
- Processing: Vector search in Qdrant using Gemini embeddings
- Output: Array of relevant textbook content chunks with metadata
- Maximum results: 5 (as specified in requirements)

## Response Format
```json
{
  "results": [
    {
      "content": "text content of the matched chunk",
      "source_file": "path to original markdown file",
      "chapter_title": "title of the chapter",
      "score": "similarity score (0.0-1.0)",
      "page_url": "URL to the original content"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Error Handling
- Returns empty results array if no relevant content is found
- Handles Qdrant connection failures gracefully
- Implements rate limiting for API calls